## 1. PID Complaint Narrative (Fully Insured Plans)

**Filed via:** PID Online Consumer Complaint Portal / Consumer Services Bureau, 1-877-881-6388

**Complaint against:** [Insurer Name] (health plan) and [Provider/Facility Name] (balance-billing entity)

---

**Narrative (portal text box):**

> I am filing this complaint regarding an unlawful out-of-network balance bill and my health plan's failure to apply No Surprises Act cost-sharing protections.
>
> On [Date(s) of Service], I received [emergency care / non-emergency care from an out-of-network ancillary provider / non-emergency care from an out-of-network provider] at [Facility Name], an in-network facility, account #[Account Number]. The provider has billed me $[Amount] above my in-network cost-sharing obligation.
>
> Under the No Surprises Act (PHSA §§ 2799A-1 – 2799A-3; 45 C.F.R. Part 149), my liability for [these services] is capped at in-network cost-sharing. [If ancillary/emergency: Balance billing for these services cannot be waived by any consent form.] [If non-emergency OON: No valid notice-and-consent waiver under 45 C.F.R. § 149.420 was provided at least 72 hours before the service; I did not sign a valid waiver.] [Attach or describe: EOB showing the amount applied; the balance bill.]
>
> On [October 1, 2024 / actual date], I submitted a written dispute to the provider via certified mail (USPS #[7020-0640-0001-2345 or actual #]) and a companion notice to my insurer (portal ref #[INS-884291-DISP or actual #]). The provider acknowledged a hold (Hold Confirmation #[HLD-55120 or actual #]), but as of [today's date], the balance remains unresolved and my account has not been corrected to in-network cost-sharing.
>
> **Requested action:** I request that the Department (1) investigate whether [Insurer] applied No Surprises Act in-network cost-sharing to this claim and (2) review the plan's compliance determination. I further request external review of the plan's compliance with the No Surprises Act's surprise-billing and cost-sharing protections under Act 146 of 2022, which gives covered persons the right to submit such a request to this Department.
>
> [If applicable:] I note that my plan's adverse determination notice did not include the Act 146 disclosure of my right to request this external review. I ask the Department to review that omission as well.
>
> I have not made any partial payment or written acknowledgment of the disputed balance, and I request that the Department confirm the account remains in dispute status with no adverse credit reporting while this complaint and review are pending.

**Attachments:** certified mail receipt, dispute letter, EOB, balance bill, provider hold confirmation, insurer portal submission confirmation.

